<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Minuit</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1580–1638</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Minuit was a Walloon-born colonial governor. As director of New Netherland from 1626 he is credited with buying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenape">Lenape</a> for goods worth sixty guilders. Recalled in 1631, he later led the Swedish expedition that founded New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-christina">Fort Christina</a> on the Delaware in 1638, and was lost at sea in a hurricane the same year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-minuit.jpg" alt="Peter Minuit" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Minuit_(Minnewit)_old_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
